# Line endings.
#
# The repo is developed on Windows and built on Linux CI. Without this file a
# Windows checkout rewrites every text file to CRLF, and two things break in
# ways that look like unrelated bugs:
#
#   1. `gofmt -l .` — the CI gate — reports every Go file as unformatted, so
#      the check stops meaning anything locally.
#   2. Shell scripts (scripts/install.sh, action/entrypoint.sh) and the
#      generated pre-commit hook must stay LF; a CRLF shebang is a confusing
#      "bad interpreter" failure on Linux and macOS.
#
# text=auto normalises on commit; the explicit eol=lf rules make the checkout
# identical on every platform for the files where it matters.
* text=auto

*.go    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.mdc   text eol=lf
*.astro text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.gif  binary
